  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 141 AM CST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nFollowing mid-level troughing over the area early this week, \nridging builds over the Desert SW mid-week and then develops over \nthe area by late week/early weekend. This allows highs to warm \nback into the 50F-65F range Wednesday as well as Thursday \n(Thanksgiving Day), 60F- 70F range Friday, and then 65F-75F range \nby Saturday as ridging peaks. Lows still falling below freezing \nfor much of the area Wednesday night will likewise only fall into \nthe 35F-45F range Thursday and Friday nights, and fail to fall \nbelow the 40F-50F range by Saturday night. Ensembles still hint at\ntroughing developing over northern MX late week/early weekend, \nbut have converged on solutions showing the troughing flattening \nout and quasi-zonal mid-level ridging building back in. The more \nquasi-zonal and subtle ridging oriented air pattern will keep \nwinds Thursday into Saturday from the W/SW and gusting to 20-30 \nmph during the afternoon leeward of the western higher terrain. \nSlightly cooler weather this Sunday will be followed by a return \nto very mild to moderately warm temperatures once more to start \nnext week. With large scale sinking and drying motion providing by\nridging aloft, we are expecting little to no chance of \nprecipitation following very brief wintry weather early this week.",
